{"t": 128.65, "n": 42, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Rows 2.1, 2.14 and the new row 2.18 are built and marked 2026-11-26. `tests/test_independent_review.py` and `tests/test_code_mode.py` ran together at 64 passed.\n\n- **2.18 (new):** I added it at the end of phase 2. It appends the five `ts-rev-*` criteria to `independent-review.spec.md` as `- [ ] <id> <text>` lines, with the exact text from `outcome.json`. The docs_check failure is gone.\n- **Docs rows for the two specs made false:** I added 3.9 (`code-join.spec.md`) and 3.10 (`overview.spec.md`) at the end of phase 3, unmarked. No row of any phase named either spec.\n- **Plan otherwise unchanged:** I changed nothing else in the plan.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_independent_review.py and tests/test_code_mode.py together: 64 passed. Added row 2.18 (docs, independent-review.spec.md, five ts-rev-* criteria as `- [ ] <id> <text>` lines with the exact outcome.json text) and built it; marked 2.1, 2.14 and 2.18. Added unmarked rows 3.9 (code-join.spec.md: code_join is now a route) and 3.10 (overview.spec.md: no review unit in its list and picture) for phase 3, as the operator decided. Deviations accepted earlier: diagram/model.json and workflow.md were regenerated by running test_parallel_reading.py -k diagram_files_follow; no calibration seed cases for ts-rev-blockers; review_after never writes \"Visit: refused\"; the arm test imports test_code_mode by name.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "59ddce64-0764-4549-a4bd-f4ab3ee17b07"}
